<%- include('/partials/head') %>

<div class="wrap page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">The process, end to end</p>
  <h1>How ReWear Works</h1>
  <p class="lede">Renting a garment from a neighbour only works if both sides know exactly what
    happens at each step. This is the whole flow.</p>
</div>

<!-- ---------- renting ---------- -->
<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Renting an outfit</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-4 mt">
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Get verified</h3>
        <p class="soft">One short form, approved by an admin. Verification is what lets members trust
          handing clothes to each other.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Find and request</h3>
        <p class="soft">Filter by category, occasion, size, locality and the dates you need. Send a
          request with your dates and a short note.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Owner decides</h3>
        <p class="soft">The owner accepts or declines. Accepting automatically declines other requests
          for the same dates, so nothing is double-booked.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">4</div><h3>Condition record</h3>
        <p class="soft">Before handover the owner photographs the item and notes any existing marks.
          You confirm you agree once it is in your hands.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">5</div><h3>Wear it</h3>
        <p class="soft">The rental runs for the dates you booked. A reminder appears on your dashboard
          two days before it is due back.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">6</div><h3>Return</h3>
        <p class="soft">Hand it back in the same locality. The owner records the return condition with
          photos.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">7</div><h3>Confirm</h3>
        <p class="soft">You confirm the return and the booking is marked complete. Deposit comes back
          to you directly.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="num">8</div><h3>Review</h3>
        <p class="soft">Both sides can now review each other. Only completed bookings can be reviewed.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ---------- the condition record ---------- -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="dash-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The part that builds trust</p>
        <h2>The condition record</h2>
        <p class="soft">Most disputes over borrowed clothes come down to one question: was that mark
          there before? ReWear answers it in writing, twice.</p>
        <ul class="trust">
          <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span><strong>Before handover</strong> &mdash; the owner
            records overall condition, visible marks, stains, tears, missing buttons, and which
            accessories are included, with photos.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span><strong>The renter confirms</strong> the record
            before the rental period starts. Nothing begins until both agree.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span><strong>On return</strong> &mdash; the owner
            records the condition again: unchanged, minor damage, major damage, or a missing item.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Both records stay attached to the booking, so the
            history is always there to look at.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Booking timeline</h3>
        <div class="timeline">
          <% ['Listed','Booked','Handed Over','Rented','Returned','Completed'].forEach((s, i) => { %>
            <div class="step <%= i < 4 ? 'done' : '' %> <%= i === 4 ? 'now' : '' %>">
              <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="l"><%= s %></span>
            </div>
          <% }) %>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">Every booking shows this timeline, so both members always know whose turn it is.</p>
        <hr>
        <h3>What ReWear does not do</h3>
        <p class="soft" style="font-size:.9rem;margin:0">No payments, no delivery, no insurance.
          Rent and deposit are settled directly between members, and handover is local and in person.
          Keeping it simple is deliberate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ---------- resale and donation ---------- -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Supporting module</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem">Reselling</h2>
        <p class="soft">List an item with an asking price. Interested members send an enquiry through
          the platform. When you accept, contact details are shared and you settle the sale between
          yourselves. Mark it handed over and the listing closes.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" href="/resale">Visit the Resale Hub</a>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Supporting module</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem">Donating</h2>
        <p class="soft">List wearable clothes with a preferred handover method. Members can request
          them, or you can take part in a collection drive listed by an administrator. The same
          accept-then-handover flow applies.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" href="/donate">Visit the Donation Hub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ---------- safety ---------- -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center" style="max-width:56ch;margin:0 auto 32px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Trust &amp; safety</p>
      <h2>What keeps this safe</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <div class="pillar"><h3>Verified members only</h3>
        <p class="soft">Browsing is open, but renting and listing need admin verification.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><h3>Limited personal information</h3>
        <p class="soft">Profiles show a name, locality and college. Phone numbers are shared only
          after a booking is accepted, and addresses never.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><h3>Reviews that mean something</h3>
        <p class="soft">A review can only be written after a completed transaction, so ratings cannot
          be manufactured.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><h3>Before and after photos</h3>
        <p class="soft">Condition is documented at both ends of every rental.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><h3>Local handover</h3>
        <p class="soft">Meetings happen in the listed locality, in a public place.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><h3>Report anything</h3>
        <p class="soft">Every listing and profile has a report option. Admins review reports and can
          remove listings.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="center mt"><a class="btn" href="/browse">Start browsing</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('/partials/foot') %>
